{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "The sole completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved 53.2% accuracy, a moderate baseline. The largest untested architectural lever is whether moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with an expressive aggregation (transformer) can meaningfully improve performance. config_012 keeps the exact same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion strategy (concat) as the baseline, isolating the effect of multiprofile + transformer aggregation. Transformer aggregation is the most expressive way to combine multiple profile representations and is the natural 'upper bound' for multiprofile; if it does not beat the singleprofile baseline, I can rule out the entire multiprofile family and redirect remaining budget toward encoder swaps (scgpt) or fusion changes. If it does help, it opens a clear exploitation path (scgpt + transformer, weighted fusion, etc.). Expected relative cost: roughly 2× the 0.62 GPU-hour baseline (~1.2–1.5 GPU hours) due to multiprofile token processing and the transformer aggregation layer, which is a reasonable investment given 8 experiments remain and this is the single most informative architectural question at this stage."
}

